    "narrative": "Our daily optimization for June 20th highlights **Lawrence Butler** as our strongest play, boasting a 74.61 score against Walbert Ure\u00f1a. His matchup is ideal for an Ottoneu roster built on efficiency; the favorable park factor and a weak SP skill matchup (+16%) create an environment for high-ceiling production. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (66.12) is locked into the starting lineup due to a significant platoon advantage and a high probability of finding the basepaths against Rea. While the optimizer is cautious about **Bryson Stott** (63.26) facing Freddy Peralta, his elevated score is driven by a high-probability stolen base scenario against a slow-delivery arm, which we must exploit given the scarcity of speed in our current build.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the exclusion of **Jeremiah Jackson**, who sits on the bench with a 40.83 score. While he faces the daunting Yoshinobu Yamamoto, his potential for late-inning impact was eclipsed by the higher-floor projections of **Tyler Freeman** and **Jung Hoo Lee**. We are intentionally keeping **Taylor Ward** active despite a marginal 45.93 score against Yamamoto; the wind conditions provide a slight boost to his power profile that narrowly kept him ahead of the bench alternatives. We continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryson Stott**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Taylor Ward**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Lawrence Butler**, as any shift in batting order could further dampen the projections for **Cal Raleigh** or **Geraldo Perdomo**, both of whom are heavily reliant on their assumed top-of-order plate appearances to generate value. \n\nOur lineup remains tempered by caution regarding the elite-arm risk posed by Yoshinobu Yamamoto to **Taylor Ward**, as well as the volatility surrounding the rest of the bottom-order bats like **Drew Gilbert**. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Dylan Beavers** all sidelined on the IL, we are forced to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. Every marginal start today is managed with the strict intent of preserving our remaining games-played cap while extracting maximum efficiency from favorable platoon splits.",
